    {
      "co": "Arcana · Workspace",
      "content": {
        "approach": "",
        "customSections": [
          {
            "body": "Institutional investors, analysts & researchers operate in a <strong>high frequency, high cognitive load environment</strong>. Their daily workflow involves simultaneously monitoring live prices, charts, news, alerts, and global market context while switching context across multiple asset classes.",
            "items": [
              "<strong>Fragmented Information</strong> — Prices, charts, news, alerts, and market hours live in separate views. Users must mentally stitch insights together by exploring each view independently.",
              "<strong>High Context Switching Cost</strong> — Switching between workflows (e.g., market open vs research) requires re-navigation. Analysts lose time reconstructing views multiple times a day.",
              "<strong>One-Size-Fits-All Interfaces</strong> — Different users track different assets, regions, and time horizons. A single default layout fails all of them.",
              "<strong>Poor State Persistence</strong> — Users expect their layouts, filters, and configurations to persist across sessions. Without this, they rework the same setup every time they log in.",
            ],
            "num": "01",
            "title": "Problem Statement",
          },
          {
            "body": null,
            "items": [
              "A modular workspace increases <strong>product stickiness</strong>. Custom dashboards directly correlate with higher retention and daily engagement by becoming the user’s <strong>first preference</strong> for daily monitoring.",
              "There is <strong>already a market precedent</strong> set by <strong>Bloomberg Launchpad</strong> — one of the most heavily used terminal features — because it solves this exact problem through customizable, persistent widgets & workspaces.",
            ],
            "num": "02",
            "title": "Why This Is Worth Solving",
          },
          {
            "body": "Build <strong>Arcana Workspace</strong> — a modular, <strong>Bloomberg-style Launchpad</strong> that allows users to create, save, and switch between personalised workspaces composed of configurable widgets — optimised for real-time monitoring, clarity, and execution with speed, leading to repeat daily usage.",
            "items": null,
            "num": "03",
            "title": "Product Vision",
          },
          {
            "body": null,
            "items": [
              "Enable users to build custom workspaces using modular widgets from scratch or premade templates",
              "Templates are workspace formats with widgets designed for unique use cases (NEWS, Portfolio, Research) — with optional Global Settings that are must-haves (e.g., Portfolio template requires selecting an index/equity to power widgets)",
              "Support adding, resizing, configuring, and saving widget layouts",
              "Allow multiple tabs/pages per workspace",
              "Ability to edit / copy / add / save / share workspace & pages, with fast switching between them",
              "Preserve widget-level intelligence (e.g., Nvidia selected in index & performance widget persists)",
              "<strong>V1 = Signal intake + context + workflow persistence.</strong> V2 = Outcome measurement (performance, deep analytics, risk, attribution, order execution integration)",
            ],
            "num": "04",
            "title": "Goals for V1",
          },
          {
            "body": "A Bloomberg Launchpad user typically combines price monitors + charts + news feeds to correlate headlines with price reactions, uses alerts to catch significant moves without continuous hovering, and saves workflows by theme (commodity tracking, earnings day, global markets). This mirrors how users segment their day:",
            "items": [
              "<strong>Morning pre-open scan</strong> — Macro indices, overnight movers, news catch-up",
              "<strong>Live session monitoring</strong> — Real-time price action, alerts firing, chart patterns",
              "<strong>Post-close analysis</strong> — P&L review, sector performance, next-day prep",
            ],
            "num": "05",
            "title": "Market Research",
          },
          {
            "body": "These cover the <strong>core workflows of watching prices & signals</strong> — the top job of users. We are launching the monitoring layer, not the outcome layer.",
            "items": null,
            "num": "06",
            "title": "Prioritised Widgets",
            "widgets": [
              {
                "name": "Equity Price Monitor",
                "rationale": "Most basic, most used — priority 1 for every workflow",
              },
              {
                "name": "Index Tracker",
                "rationale": "Global indices (S&P, Nifty) — macro sentiment gauge widely used by analysts",
              },
              {
                "name": "Commodity Prices",
                "rationale": "Critical for cross-asset views (similar to Bloomberg’s commodities widget)",
              },
              {
                "name": "Real-Time Chart",
                "rationale": "Visual confirmation of trends & patterns — core to all workflows",
              },
              {
                "name": "Live News Feed",
                "rationale": "Provides context to price movements — heavily used across all personas",
              },
              {
                "name": "Price Alerts",
                "rationale": "Simple price threshold alerts — helps catch key events without always watching",
              },
              {
                "name": "Timezone / Market Hours",
                "rationale": "Supports a global view across regions and trading sessions",
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            "body": null,
            "items": null,
            "num": "07",
            "subsections": [
              {
                "items": [
                  "Grid-based canvas (like Metabase dashboard layout) — chosen over free-form positioning to optimise for scale, stability, and cognitive clarity in high-load environments",
                  "Preset templates for core use cases (Portfolio Analysis, Single Stock Analysis, etc.) with pre-specified widgets and optional Global Settings",
                  "Workspaces can be copied, renamed, shared, rearranged, customised and managed from settings",
                  "Added workspaces appear side-by-side and switch instantly on click",
                ],
                "title": "Workspace",
              },
              {
                "items": [
                  "Modular, atomic blocks of the workspace with multiple responsive UI sizes (like Apple widgets — different UI for different grid sizes)",
                  "Can be configured (columns/filters/indicators/flags), added, resized, repositioned, renamed, or removed",
                  "Widgets retain their full capabilities inside the workspace (e.g., Summary widget retains % AUM & % Gross selections)",
                  "Users can add any widget from the terminal directly to a workspace page; widget lands in the next vacant grid area",
                  "Widgets cannot overlap. Option to export widget data in relevant Excel format",
                ],
                "title": "Widgets",
              },
              {
                "items": [
                  "Each workspace supports multiple pages representing sub-contexts (e.g., Price, Valuation within a Portfolio template)",
                  "Pages visible side-by-side with add, delete, reorder, rename, copy, share capabilities",
                  "Pages can be managed from settings or via right-click context menu",
                ],
                "title": "Pages",
              },
              {
                "items": [
                  "V1: Global Settings for presets — groupings are done during template creation (e.g., selecting a stock links all widgets)",
                  "V2: Fully-fledged Group Manager where users can map components to each other, change a security in one component and all grouped components update",
                ],
                "title": "Group Components (V1 → V2)",
              },
            ],
            "title": "Core Capabilities",
          },
          {
            "body": null,
            "items": null,
            "journeys": [
              {
                "entry": "No existing workspaces",
                "exit": "Saved workspace with at least one page and widget",
                "name": "First-Time User Experience",
                "steps": [
                  "User opens Arcana Workspace, clicks Create New → 3 options: optimised view for screen, sample view from manager, or blank canvas",
                  "On blank canvas: Launchpad toolbar appears with Page 1 and no widgets. Search bar available to add components or select templates",
                  "User adds first component or selects template, configures parameters/global settings, adjusts position & size",
                  "User saves the view and workspace",
                ],
              },
              {
                "entry": "Active workspace with at least one page",
                "exit": "Configured widget on active page",
                "name": "Adding & Configuring a Widget",
                "steps": [
                  "User clicks search → Component/Template Browser opens with categories and previews",
                  "Selects component → appears on canvas in default state",
                  "User configures columns/filters/indicators/flags, optionally renames widget",
                  "A widget can’t exist in the same state twice on a particular page",
                ],
              },
              {
                "entry": "Workspace with at least one saved page",
                "exit": "One workspace, multiple task-specific pages",
                "name": "Building a Multi-Page Workspace",
                "steps": [
                  "User clicks +New Page, creates Page 2 inside the same workspace",
                  "Adds different widgets (e.g., Asia markets) or templates from search",
                  "Right-click options: copy, rename, rearrange, delete, share, customise",
                  "Pages appear side-by-side, switch instantly on click",
                ],
              },
              {
                "entry": "Existing saved workspaces",
                "exit": "Updated workspace state persisted for next session",
                "name": "Returning User Daily Flow",
                "steps": [
                  "User logs in → last-used workspace auto-opens (if no default set)",
                  "Scans monitors, switches pages/workspaces as needed",
                  "Makes minor edits → auto-save or manual save persists state",
                ],
              },
            ],
            "num": "08",
            "title": "User Journeys",
          },
          {
            "body": null,
            "items": null,
            "metricGroups": [
              {
                "metrics": [
                  {
                    "definition": "% of active users who create ≥1 workspace within 7 days",
                    "metric": "Workspace Creation Rate",
                    "why": "Indicates initial value discovery",
                  },
                  {
                    "definition": "% of users who create a workspace, add ≥3 widgets & save it",
                    "metric": "Activation Rate",
                    "why": "Confirms meaningful usage, not just exploration",
                  },
                  {
                    "definition": "% of users using a template vs blank canvas",
                    "metric": "Template Usage Rate",
                    "why": "Validates usefulness of templates",
                  },
                  {
                    "definition": "% of users who abandon creation flow before saving",
                    "metric": "Creation Drop-off Rate",
                    "why": "Identifies friction in workspace creation",
                  },
                ],
                "name": "Adoption & Activation",
                "subtitle": "Is Workspace Valuable?",
              },
              {
                "metrics": [
                  {
                    "definition": "Workspace DAU ÷ Total DAU",
                    "metric": "Workspace DAU Ratio",
                    "why": "Indicates daily stickiness",
                  },
                  {
                    "definition": "% of sessions where Workspace opens by default",
                    "metric": "Default Launch Rate",
                    "why": "Signals habit formation",
                  },
                  {
                    "definition": "Avg workspace sessions per user per day ÷ total sessions",
                    "metric": "Repeat Usage Rate",
                    "why": "Measures frequency of use",
                  },
                  {
                    "definition": "Day-over-day retention for Workspace users",
                    "metric": "D1–D30 Retention",
                    "why": "Validates long-term platform stickiness",
                  },
                  {
                    "definition": "Average widgets added per workspace",
                    "metric": "Avg Widgets per Workspace",
                    "why": "Indicates richness of setup",
                  },
                  {
                    "definition": "% of users switching pages within a session",
                    "metric": "Page Switching Rate",
                    "why": "Validates page-level value",
                  },
                ],
                "name": "Engagement & Habit Formation",
                "subtitle": "Is It Becoming a Daily Tool?",
              },
            ],
            "num": "09",
            "title": "Success Metrics",
          },
        ],
        "impact": {
          "items": [],
          "text": "",
